msgstr "這些方法會形成伺服器的客戶端 I/O 循環，並確保連線的 TCP 用戶端進行可靠的訊息交換。"

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Server_APIs.rst:528
#: 8936cbe70fcf44ac9cabec9e38c0195d
#, fuzzy
msgid "TCP Server inbound event listener API"
msgstr "TCP伺服器檔案傳輸API"

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Server_APIs.rst:530
#: 583ef0a34dfc480da5b4fc87108cbf2f
msgid "External code can observe traffic without replacing the protocol loop:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Server_APIs.rst:540
#: 0a30ecd70b364968a892136d9bec809f
msgid ""
"``add_message_listener`` registers ``listener(client_id, message)`` for "
"every inbound line, commands included (``/help``, ``/file ...``, the "
"crypto handshake lines, ...), so a listener observes all inbound traffic;"
" line dispatch is unaffected, a command still goes to the command "
"handlers. ``add_file_listener`` registers ``listener(client_id, "
"full_path, name, size, command)`` and fires after a file uploaded by a "
"client has been fully written to the transfer directory (``command`` is "
"the wire command that triggered it, so protocol pushes such as "
"``/crypto_pub_key`` can be recognised). Both listeners run on a protocol "
"thread, so they must not block, and an exception inside a listener is "
"logged and swallowed. The ``remove_*`` counterparts unregister a listener"
" and ignore unknown ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Server_APIs.rst:553
#: a7bb1a9276bd4860882ffd43a680d6bf
msgid ""
"In addition, received messages and events are stored per sender socket in"
" ``messages_dict`` / ``events_dict`` (each entry a ``[content, "
"timestamp]`` pair). When a store reaches ``max_dict_size`` (64 KiB) it is"
" flushed to ``messages_log.json`` / ``events_log.json`` under "
"``network_api/.Flow`` and cleared; ``stop`` flushes both stores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Server_APIs.rst:562
